Q7. Can we overload the constructor in a class?
Ans. Yes we can overload constructor in a class, maybe if we want constructor with different parameter. 
Example: 

public class Box {
    double width;
    double height;
    double depth;

    // Constructor with all dimensions
    public Box(double w, double h, double d) {
        width = w;
        height = h;
        depth = d;
    }

    // Constructor for a cube (all dimensions equal)
    public Box(double side) {
        width = height = depth = side;
    }

    // Default constructor (no arguments)
    public Box() {
        width = -1; // Indicate uninitialized
        height = -1;
        depth = -1;
    }
}

